Chapter: E1000LcdReload
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci
  cites Dev chapter NicAsde

 THE OBLIGATION IS CITED AND IT IS ABOUT A RESET WE ISSUE. I219 rev 2.02
 section 5.2, "Reset Operation", under PHY Soft Reset: "A PHY reset caused by
 writing to bit 15 in MDIO register 0. Setting the bit resets the PHY, but
 does not reset non-PHY parts. The PHY registers are reset, but other I219
 registers are not." Then the sentence that makes it a driver action rather
 than a description: "The integrated LAN controller configures the LCD
 registers."

 So every path that writes BMCR bit 15 owes the LCD configuration afterwards.
 `e1000-init` pays it by construction, because `e1000-pch-prepare` runs after
 `e1000-init-at` returns and therefore after the bring-up reset. This arm asks
 the question about the OTHER path: `na-phy-kick` resets the PHY for the ASDE
 arms and nothing reconfigures behind it.

 IT IS A DIFFERENT QUESTION FROM `i219-k1-mechanism`, which resets through
 `e1000-phy-bring-up` and reconfigures with a bare `e1000-k1-configure`. Both
 halves there are the arm's own calls, so it measures the register and the
 stall. This one puts a DRIVER FUNCTION on the kill side, so the row moves if
 that function ever starts reloading and moves back if it stops.

Section: Fixtures

  i219-pm-page : Integer = 770
  i219-pm-reg : Integer = 17

  dev-id-of : PciScanResult -> Integer
  dev-id-of (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> (d.pci-device-id)
      is None -> 0

  bring-up : PciScanResult -> E1000Device
  bring-up (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> e1000-init d
      is None -> e1000-absent

  mk-frame : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mk-frame (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc else mk-frame (i + 1) n (list-push acc i)

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  pm-read : Integer -> Integer
  pm-read (mmio) =
   let p = e1000-phy-set-page mmio i219-pm-page
   in let v = e1000-phy-read mmio i219-pm-reg
   in let b = e1000-phy-set-page mmio 0
   in v

Section: Entry

 THE LADDER LEADS WITH A KILL AND THE ARM MANUFACTURES BOTH SIDES. The kill
 is `na-bring-up-after`, which is the ASDE bring-up minus the MAC reset:
 `na-bring-up` would reset the MAC as well and a send that failed after it
 could be failing for the rings rather than for K1, which is the confounder
 `e1000-pch-k1` avoids the same way. The pass is `e1000-pch-prepare`, called
 with `True` rather than with `e1000-pch-k1-required` so that this stays a
 pair whatever that constant ships as.

 `gate answers` is the omission point read from the shipped build:
 `e1000-lcd-reload` answers 0 while `e1000-pch-lcd-reload-required` is False,
 and `e1000-pch-prepare`'s own four answers once it is True. The row moves the
 day the constant flips, which is what a named omission point is for.

 `770.17 left by init` is read FIRST and printed second, and it is evidence
 about the shipped path: the value there is the configured one, which is what
 "e1000-init pays the obligation by construction" means when measured rather
 than argued.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in let did = dev-id-of scan
    in let d = bring-up scan
    in let mmio = d.e-mmio
    in let at-init = pm-read mmio
    in let kick1 = na-bring-up-after mmio did False
    in let after-kick1 = pm-read mmio
    in let send-kick1 = e1000-send-frame d (mk-frame 0 64 [])
    in let reload1 = e1000-pch-prepare mmio did True
    in let after-reload1 = pm-read mmio
    in let send-reload1 = e1000-send-frame d (mk-frame 0 64 [])
    in let kick2 = na-bring-up-after mmio did False
    in let after-kick2 = pm-read mmio
    in let send-kick2 = e1000-send-frame d (mk-frame 0 64 [])
    in let reload2 = e1000-pch-prepare mmio did True
    in let after-reload2 = pm-read mmio
    in let send-reload2 = e1000-send-frame d (mk-frame 0 64 [])
    in let gate = e1000-lcd-reload mmio did
    in act
      print-line-uni ("part is pch        : " & yn (e1000-pch-part did))
      print-line-uni ("shipped reload step: " & yn e1000-pch-lcd-reload-required)
      print-line-uni ("770.17 left by init: " & show at-init)
      print-line-uni ("1 kill after kick  : " & show after-kick1)
      print-line-uni ("  send             : " & show send-kick1)
      print-line-uni ("2 pass after reload: " & show after-reload1)
      print-line-uni ("  send             : " & show send-reload1)
      print-line-uni ("3 kill after kick  : " & show after-kick2)
      print-line-uni ("  send             : " & show send-kick2)
      print-line-uni ("4 pass after reload: " & show after-reload2)
      print-line-uni ("  send             : " & show send-reload2)
      print-line-uni ("prepare answers    : " & show reload2)
      print-line-uni ("gate answers       : " & show gate)
    end
  end

